Pre-season is the hardest part of a rugby year. Long sessions, contact coming back, and young bodies doing far more than they did over summer.

The Otago Boys' High School 1st XV use X-ZONE through their pre-season. {OBHS_DETAILS}

What a good school programme gets right: the load builds slowly, warm-ups are not optional, and knocks get reported early, not hidden. Any head knock means off the field and a proper medical check, every time.

